    /* ── Make the CSV card the SAME height as the JSON card (LAYOUT ONLY) ──
       The grid already stretches both columns to one equal (tall) height, but
       the CSV card was staying short because the wrapper <div slot="output">
       never grew to fill its column, so the card kept its content height.
       We grow every link with FLEX (never percentage heights — those silently
       collapse to "auto" when the parent has no explicit height):
         .workspace-col  (stretched equal by the grid)
           → .ws-fill    (flex:1, itself a flex column)
             → the Card  (flex:1 via `.ws-fill > *` → reliably fills wrapper)
       `margin-top:auto` on the OUTPUT editor then eats exactly the slack the
       upload box creates on the JSON side, so the two editors line up at the
       top AND the bottom — empty or full, forever. No pixel values involved,
       so it self-balances and can never drift. The middle Options card is
       untouched (its wrapper has no .ws-fill, so it keeps its natural height). */
    .ws-fill {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      min-height: 0;
